<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I am sure that <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Shinju</span> will play very nice!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Felix</span> replies, putting his arm around the smirking boy. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’ll be on my best behavior. I promise I won’t try anything dastardly.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Shinju</span> says sweetly, before quietly adding, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Unless it’s funny.”</span> <span style="color:LightGreen">It takes some further convincing, but <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> eventually agrees and the four of you start a soccer match.</span> <br>
<br>

<<linkreplace"Continue">>
    The game is intense, furiously so, though not from either you or <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Felix</span>. Both of you treat it like a friendly match, laughing, playing around, not trying too hard. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Shinju</span> and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span>, however, treat it like some sort of soccer death match. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Shinju</span> is like a cat chasing the ball, pouncing on every opening he sees and putting as much pressure on <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> as he can. <br>
    <br>
    <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span>, for his part, keeps up. You had no idea he was so athletic! Or, that he can at least seem like he is. But he quickly starts to tire out and slow down, pushing himself too far in a desperate attempt to win. <span style="color:Pink">But it is as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> steals the ball from <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Shinju</span>, causing the boy to trip and roll, that you notice something that neither of the other two seem to have noticed yet. <br>

